  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most important first step is to establish a clear, interpretable baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest possible RNA-only configuration: no image processing, no learned encoder, single profile, no aggregation or fusion. It gives a performance floor against which every other design choice (image modality, learned encoders, multiprofile, aggregation, fusion) can be measured. It is also computationally cheap, leaving budget for more complex experiments later. Testing this baseline first reduces uncertainty about the RNA signal strength and the cost of added complexity, and provides the reference point needed to interpret all subsequent comparisons in the remaining 9 experiments."
}

